# Who has to approve what.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Why this file exists
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Without it, nothing distinguishes "a developer changing application code" from
# "someone changing the pipeline that decides whether application code ships".
# The second is the more dangerous edit, and until now it took the same zero
# approvals as the first.
#
# The Trivy gate, the eleven repository invariants and the "no kubectl in CI"
# rule all live in .github/workflows/ and scripts/. A single-line change there
# turns any of them off, and the diff looks small.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This file alone changes nothing
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# CODEOWNERS only takes effect where a pull request is required and reviews are
# enforced. On this repository, as of this commit:
#
#   branch protection on main : NOT configured  (API reports protected: false)
#   pull requests opened      : 0
#   commits on main           : 59, all pushed directly
#
# So this file states the intended ownership boundary and will start enforcing it
# the moment branch protection is switched on. The steps are in
# .github/workflows/README.md. Committing the intent first is deliberate — the
# boundary is a design decision and belongs in review, not in a settings page
# nobody reads.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Placeholders
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# @app-team and @platform-team do not exist. This repository has one author, and
# inventing GitHub teams that resolve to nobody would make every PR unmergeable
# while looking correct. Replace them with real teams or usernames when there is
# more than one person; the paths and the split are the part worth reviewing.

# ── Default ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything not matched below. Later rules win, so this is only a floor.
*                                   @platform-team

# ── Application code ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The app team owns what the service does.
/app/                               @app-team
/docker/                            @app-team @platform-team

# ── What developers are meant to change without a platform review ───────────
# This is the whole point of the Kustomize base/overlay split: tunable values
# live in the overlay, so adjusting them is not a platform change.
/k8s/overlays/dev/                  @app-team
/k8s/overlays/prod/config.env       @app-team
/k8s/overlays/prod/patches/         @app-team

# ── Delivery and platform: platform review required ─────────────────────────
# k8s/base holds the securityContext, the probes, the PDB and the rollout
# strategy. Those are the guarantees, not tunables.
/k8s/base/                          @platform-team

# The pipeline that decides what ships, and the gates inside it.
/.github/                           @platform-team
/scripts/                           @platform-team

# Infrastructure. A change here can delete a cluster; see the human gate in
# .github/workflows/terraform.yaml.
/infra/                             @platform-team

# Delivery and observability configuration.
/argocd/                            @platform-team
/observability/                     @platform-team

# Ansible manages VMs outside the cluster.
/ansible/                           @platform-team

# ── The rules about the rules ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Changing the spec, the ignore rules, or the line-ending policy changes what
# every other check means.
/CLAUDE.md                          @platform-team
/.gitignore                         @platform-team
/.gitattributes                     @platform-team
/.trivyignore                       @platform-team
/.yamllint.yml                      @platform-team
/trivy.yaml                         @platform-team

# ── Deliberately NOT restricted ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Documentation. A stale document is a real problem — three were found in this
# project — and requiring a platform review to fix a wrong sentence is how they
# stay wrong.
/README.md                          @app-team @platform-team
/EVIDENCE.md                        @app-team @platform-team
/RUNBOOK.md                         @app-team @platform-team
